;; DECOMP BEGINS

;; get-player-amplitude: honest stub, issue 759, a2 rung's own STEP 3. This
;; object's own group (decompiler/config/jakx/all-types.gc's own
;; net-mgr-medius-players comment block) places it beside add-recent-
;; opponent, get-recent-players, medius-player-info-retrieve-behavior,
;; update-client-state and init-player-lists - every one of them still a
;; provisional extern with no defun anywhere in this tree (issue 759's own
;; plan table D). Its true body would read a live Medius voice-chat signal
;; level for the player its own argument names (the row-text donor passes a
;; player-name string's own char data, str+4, per menu2.gc:5792-5798's own
;; raw disasm), which is the whole unlanded online subsystem this file's own
;; group belongs to, not a same-commit fix. Stubbed to a constant 0.0
;; (silent/no-amplitude) so base-menu-method-60 (string-menu)'s own 858-line
;; draw method, which calls this once per visible row, is a real linked call
;; rather than a jump to address 0 the first time it runs. Retire this stub
;; once net-mgr-medius-players' own real player-list query lands and can
;; supply a genuine per-player amplitude reading.
(defun get-player-amplitude ((arg0 object))
  0.0
  )

